      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AZHXA",
      "text": "(B), (C) and (D) only",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Net force on proton inside an electric and a magnetic field is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mi>F</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mover><mi>F</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi><mfenced><mrow><mover><mi>v</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>×</mo><mover><mi>B</mi><mo>→</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>If both <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>→</mo></mover></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>B</mi><mo>→</mo></mover></math> are zero, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mi>F</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mi>e</mi></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mi>F</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub></math> both are zero. Hence, velocity may remain constant. Therefore, option (A) is correct.</p><p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>B</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, but velocity is parallel or antiparallel to the magnetic field, then also <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mi>F</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mi>e</mi></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mi>F</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub></math> both are zero. Hence, option (B) is also correct.</p><p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>B</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, but <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mi>F</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mi>e</mi></msub><mo> </mo><mo>+</mo><mo> </mo><msub><mover><mi>F</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, then also velocity may remain constant. Thus, option (D) is also correct.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
